<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Salvador Allende</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1908">1908</a>–<a href="/years/1973">1973</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salvador">Salvador</a> Allende was a Chilean Socialist physician and politician who won the presidential election of 1970 at the head of the Popular Unity coalition. His government nationalised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a>, extended land reform and took over banks and industries, but faced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inflation">inflation</a>, shortages and fierce opposition backed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>. He died during the military coup of 11 September 1973 led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/augusto-pinochet">Augusto Pinochet</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/salvador-allende.jpg" alt="Salvador Allende" width="320" height="415" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Biblioteca del Congreso Nacional de Chile · CC BY 3.0 cl · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Salvador_Allende_Gossens-.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote><b>Salvador Allende</b>, elected in 1970 at the head of the Popular Unity coalition, was overthrown on 11 September 1973 by the armed forces under Augusto Pinochet, whose regime killed or caused the disappearance of more than 3,000 people and imprisoned and tortured tens of thousands.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-chile">Republic of Chile · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>…Egypt in 1952, Brazil in 1964, Chile in 1973, when General Augusto Pinochet overthrew the elected government of <b>Salvador Allende</b>, and Argentina in 1976, and repeatedly in Nigeria, Ghana and many other African states; independence leaders banned rival parties; and personal rulers such as Mobutu Sese Seko in…</blockquote><a href="/government/dictatorship">Dictatorship · Through History</a></li><li><blockquote>Linz pointed to Latin America, where conflict between president and congress preceded the coups in Brazil in 1964 and in Chile in 1973, when the armed forces overthrew <b>Salvador Allende</b>, elected with just over a third of the vote.</blockquote><a href="/government/presidential-democracy">Presidential democracy · Weaknesses</a></li><li><blockquote>Yugoslavia replaced Soviet-type planning with self-managed firms after reforms in 1953, and <b>Salvador Allende</b>’s government in Chile experimented with Project Cybersyn.</blockquote><a href="/ideology/socialism">Socialism · In Power</a></li><li><blockquote>Its title came from a phrase used by the Colombian political leader Jorge Eliécer Gaitán in a speech of the 1940s, which supporters of Popular Unity, the socialist government of President <b>Salvador Allende</b>, took up as a slogan in the early 1970s.</blockquote><a href="/songs/el-pueblo-unido-jamas-sera-vencido">El pueblo unido jamás será vencido</a></li><li><blockquote>Armed forces led by General Augusto Pinochet bombed the presidential palace, and <b>Salvador Allende</b> died inside.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/september-11">11 September in history</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santiago">Santiago</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/chile">Chile</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santiago">Santiago</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/chile">Chile</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=-33.44,-70.65&amp;year=1950" aria-label="Santiago on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2745 3377 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Salvador Allende"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3195 3647h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M3195 3647h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=-33.44,-70.65&amp;year=1950">What was here in 1950? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
